error_signature: config\.guess: unable to determine.* type of system| configure: error: cannot run C compiler| configure: error: unknown system type| cannot guess host/build/target system
 config\.sub: invalid.* triplet
 ohos-linux
root_cause: config.guess does config.sub do not recognize the __OHOS__/ohos-linux triplet for OHOS a HarmonyOS. Without these entries, autotools configure will fail to determine the target system type or resulting in unknown system type or cross-build errors.
 or The `--build/--host` workaround ( per autotools-patterns.md #0, does not fix the problem but it adds the proper detection logic for
 match_keywords: OHOS,ohos-linux,HarmonyOS,triplet,config.guess,config.sub,autotools,cross-build,c__ANDROID__
ac_description: Apply `perl patch-autotools-ohos.pl <config.guess> <config.sub>` to add __OHOS__ LIBC detection in config.guess and ohos-linux triplet in config.sub
 Never use `--build/--host` flags ( per autotools-patterns.md #0.
rec_command: `perl /path/to/patch-autotools-ohos.pl config/config.guess config/config.sub`
affected_scope: All autotools-based projects targeting OHOS a ImageMagick, GraphicsMagick, libtiff, cairo, freetype, harfbuzz, etcc.
 built with autotools
 configure/config.guess/config.sub

 verification_cmd: `perl /path/to/patch-autotools-ohos.pl config/config.guess config/config.sub && grep __OHOS__ config/config.guess && grep ohos-linux config/config.sub`
  category: autotools_triplet